{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"account-default","id":"msg_011CgyowhLJy6tTSGHYPfbWR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016LW5HfxUBp4jRtz4rfwA4v","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"verdict":"block","reasons":["aws_s3_bucket.buyer_records is planned as delete+create in prod. S3 bucket names can't be changed in place, so renaming 'tallowmark-prod-buyer-records' to 'tallowmark-prod-buyer-records-v2' forces Terraform to replace the bucket. The old bucket and everything in it would be destroyed.","Buyer data loss can't be undone. Versioning on the existing bucket is currently 'Suspended', so this plan may leave no versioned history to recover deleted objects from.","Your rules only allow approval for plans that only add or tag resources and don't touch buyer records. This plan deletes a resource and changes the buyer records bucket, so it can't be approved.","This isn't the lifecycle-expiry exception either. That covers expiring old telemetry or scan readings, not replacing the buyer records bucket.","Nothing here touches IAM or a database, so the wildcard and database rules don't apply. The block is for the destructive replacement of buyer PII storage.","Turning versioning from Suspended to Enabled is a good change on its own. Resubmit it as a separate plan without the bucket rename.","To get the plan through: keep the existing bucket name. If a v2 bucket is truly needed, add it as a new resource, copy the data across with verification, and plan the old bucket's removal separately with a person's sign-off. Adding lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true } to the buyer records bucket would stop this from happening again."]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":3546,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92c01eec-0f20-4475-bfa7-478cf687907f","uuid":"2d885a3f-9dd1-4598-9c57-d042df4d1baa","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22:18:55.540Z","request_id":"req_011Cgyowh7fZDvcviBTcP7jz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016LW5HfxUBp4jRtz4rfwA4v":{"verdict":"block","reasons":["aws_s3_bucket.buyer_records is planned as delete+create in prod. S3 bucket names can't be changed in place, so renaming 'tallowmark-prod-buyer-records' to 'tallowmark-prod-buyer-records-v2' forces Terraform to replace the bucket. The old bucket and everything in it would be destroyed.","Buyer data loss can't be undone. Versioning on the existing bucket is currently 'Suspended', so this plan may leave no versioned history to recover deleted objects from.","Your rules only allow approval for plans that only add or tag resources and don't touch buyer records. This plan deletes a resource and changes the buyer records bucket, so it can't be approved.","This isn't the lifecycle-expiry exception either. That covers expiring old telemetry or scan readings, not replacing the buyer records bucket.","Nothing here touches IAM or a database, so the wildcard and database rules don't apply. The block is for the destructive replacement of buyer PII storage.","Turning versioning from Suspended to Enabled is a good change on its own. Resubmit it as a separate plan without the bucket rename.","To get the plan through: keep the existing bucket name. If a v2 bucket is truly needed, add it as a new resource, copy the data across with verification, and plan the old bucket's removal separately with a person's sign-off. Adding lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true } to the buyer records bucket would stop this from happening again."]}}}
